# Plan: Layout persistence on Cloudflare (Workers + D1) with a public demo on Pages

## 1. Context and goals

DropUI currently keeps everything in memory (`BuilderStore`: `paletteItems`, `canvasElements`). A reload loses the layout. Goals:

- **Persist each visitor's canvas** (ordered list of `{ type, text }` elements) so a reload or a later visit restores it.
- **Public demo for employers**: free tier, no signup, no cold starts or "project paused" pages, and visitors cannot read each other's data.
- **One backend, many frontends**: the Angular app will be rewritten in React, Vue, Svelte and others as separate projects on separate hosts. The backend therefore exposes a small, documented REST contract (`docs/backend-contract.md`) that does not depend on any framework, plus a CORS allowlist.
- **Angular stays backend-agnostic**: the store talks to a `LayoutRepository` abstraction. HTTP is one implementation, localStorage is another (used by e2e), and an in-memory fake is used by the tests. No test hits live Cloudflare.

### Decisions at a glance

| Topic | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Compute | **One Cloudflare Worker** (`drop-ui-api`, TypeScript + **Hono**) | V8 isolates, no sleeping, cold starts measured in milliseconds, 100k req/day free |
| Storage | **D1** (SQLite), one `layouts` table, migrations via wrangler | Strongly consistent read-after-write, 100k row writes/day free; KV allows only ~1k writes/day free and is eventually consistent (up to ~60 s), which breaks "save, reload, see it" |
| Identity | **Server-issued anonymous owner id + HMAC-signed bearer token** (`POST /api/session`) | No signup. The server picks the ids (clients can't choose or enumerate them). Stateless (no DB write per session), and the secret can be rotated |
| Transport auth | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, **no cookies** | `*.pages.dev` and `*.workers.dev` are different sites, so third-party cookie blocking would break cookies. Bearer tokens work the same in every framework |
| Hosting topology | **API is its own Worker on its own origin, with CORS.** Frontend on **Cloudflare Pages** | Every framework port can point at the same API. Pages gives git-integrated builds and `*.<project>.pages.dev` preview URLs for free |
| Data format | `{ "version": 1, "elements": [{ "id", "type", "text" }] }` stored as canonical JSON text | Same shape as the sibling Supabase plan. Versioned for future migrations |

